<iscomment>
    PayPal V2 button container.

    The element id and the matching error-message id are now provided by the caller via the
    `paypalButtonId` and `paypalErrorId` template variables, instead of being hard-coded.

    Why: the PayPal V2 button can be rendered in two different placements during the same
    checkout (in the payment tab via hiPayContent.isml, and on the place-order step via
    checkout.isml). When the template hard-coded a single id, the second occurrence collided
    with the first one in the DOM, the HiPay JS SDK could not figure out which container to
    mount on, and the error message div was shared/clobbered between the two placements.

    Dedicated ids (`paypal-button-submit-payment` / `paypal-button-place-order` and their
    matching error message ids) let the client-side code (paypalV2.js, billing.js,
    hipayPaymentHelper.js) target the right container for the active placement and pick the
    currently visible error container via the `js-hipay-paypalv2-error-message` class hook.

    The error container is rendered before the button so a server-side error message remains
    visible when the button reflows or re-renders.
</iscomment>
<div id="${paypalErrorId}" class="js-hipay-paypalv2-error-message paypal-error-message"></div>
<div id="${paypalButtonId}" class="js-hipay-paypalv2-button" data-total="${pdict.total}"></div>